OPTIMIZATION 2: STACK FIX (src/reg_stack.h)

WHY
- perf after Opt 1 (diabetes): execute_kernel was 80% of runtime.
- Inside it: push 39.5%, evaluate_node 22.2%, pop 10.3%.

PROBLEM
- push looped over all 20 slots (MaxSize) with a compare each time, just to write one value.
- pop looped from the bottom up until it found the top.

CHANGE
- Replaced with a normal array + index:
  push: if (elements_ < MaxSize) regs_[elements_++] = val;
  pop:  if (elements_ > 0) return regs_[--elements_]; return 0;

RESULTS (Opt 1 -> Opt 2, speedup; total speedup vs baseline)
- diabetes:    5.05 s -> 1.32 s (3.8x); total 15.5x
- cancer:      34.5 s -> 18.1 s (1.9x); total 7.1x
- housing:     58.7 s -> 20.5 s (2.9x); total 11.8x
- silk-wave:   84.1 s -> 31.0 s (2.7x); total 12.6x
- square-wave: 262.7 s -> 97.7 s (2.7x); total 12.4x

CORRECTNESS
- MSE output identical to Opt 1 (diff empty). Only data storage changed, no math.

OBSERVATIONS
- A small code change gave a bigger speedup than all compiler flags combined, found directly from the profile.
- Cancer improved least (1.9x): something outside execute_kernel likely takes a bigger share there (possibly the logLoss metric, since it's the only classification task). To check with perf.
